    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This past year, new enhancement and tools have been added to DYNEL in order to improve the restoration of geological structures. In this contribution we describe, through examples, these new functionalities. A texture mapping tool has been added to allow the visualization of the deformed image (i.e. 2-D or 3-D reflection seismic data) associated with the finite element mesh. An algorithm has been developed to automatically correct the interpreted geometry of the structures according to criteria chosen by the user. Volumetric deformation has been implemented in order to address the restoration of 3-D structures. These enhancements push the restoration of geological structures well beyond industry standards by computing deformation between the restored and the deformed states in areas that have undergone large strains at subseismic reservoir scales.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
